{
  "abstract": "The ordinary generating function A(x) of OEIS A396843, with A(0) = 0 and A'(0) = 1, satisfies A(x A(x) − 3x A(x)^2) = x^2. The package proves that this equation has exactly one integer power-series solution and that every term a(n) with n ≥ 1 is odd, as conjectured by Paul D. Hanna (OEIS A396843, 2026). An earlier Lean proof of the oddness is in the-omega-institute/trureturing PR #6773.",
